<!--
  rules.xml - OpenClinica 3.17 Rules for study S_BJTDEMO (BJT-DEMO-01).
  100% SYNTHETIC demo content; no real study or PHI.

  Upload MANUALLY in the OC UI: Tasks -> Monitor and Manage Data -> Rules ->
  "Create New Rule(s)" (XML upload). Do this AFTER the study, events and CRF
  versions exist (the upload validates every Target/Expression OID against the
  live study) and BEFORE running seed.py. See edc/README.md step 5.

  WHY RULES (and not CRF edit checks): source-verified OC 3.17.2 behavior.
  Soft edit checks (CRF VALIDATION column / ODM RangeCheck) cause the ENTIRE
  SOAP importData call to Fail - nothing is written - so they cannot coexist
  with deliberately messy seed data. Rules with a DiscrepancyNoteAction and
  Run ImportDataEntry="true" DO run during SOAP import and auto-create open
  "Failed Validation Check" discrepancy notes on the target item
  (DataEndpoint -> DataImportService.runRulesSetup -> ImportDataRuleRunner ->
  DiscrepancyNoteActionProcessor.saveFieldNotes). Every action below therefore
  carries Run ImportDataEntry="true".

  DEDUP CAVEAT (matters for demo resets): ImportDataRuleRunner consults
  rule_action_run_log and drops an action that already ran for the same
  item + value + rule (RuleActionRunLogBean). Re-importing the same seed file
  cannot re-create the notes - resets must restore the database instead
  (edc/reset_demo.sh).

  EXPRESSION MECHANICS RELIED ON (all verified in the 3.17.2 source):
  * Partial expressions (bare item OIDs, e.g. "I_LABS_HGB gt 20") resolve
    against the values in the CURRENT import first, then the DB - so a rule
    fires in the same importData call that carries the bad value.
  * Full-path references to ANOTHER event (the date-order rule's
    SE_SCREENING....I_DEMOG_SCREENDATE) resolve from the DB only. seed.py
    therefore imports each subject's Screening event in its own SOAP call
    BEFORE the visit events, so the screening date is committed by the time
    the visit-date rule is evaluated.
  * A relational/arithmetic operator on an empty value raises
    OpenClinicaSystemException inside the rule runner, which skips that rule
    for that subject (no note, no import failure). Range rules are thus safe
    on missing values; the explicit eq "" rules handle emptiness.
  * "date lt date" compares yyyy-MM-dd dates; a blank date on either side of
    lt yields a non-"true" sentinel and the action does not fire.

  RULE INVENTORY (10 RuleDefs, 18 assignments):
    Range      : R_SBP_RANGE, R_WEIGHT_RANGE, R_HGB_RANGE, R_WBC_RANGE,
                 R_CREAT_RANGE
    Cross-field: R_WEIGHT_BMI   (weight vs site-calculated BMI + height)
                 R_VISITDATE_ORDER (visit date before screening/consent date;
                 screening CRF is the authoritative anchor)
    Empty-field: R_DBP_MISSING, R_SEX_MISSING, R_HGB_MISSING
  Schema: core/src/main/resources/properties/rules.xsd (RuleImport = all
  RuleAssignment elements first, then all RuleDef elements).
-->
